wers  of the world like dianko and luffy just  beat one before he became a warlord  crocodile had a bounty of 81 million the  former bounty suggests it might be even  higher by now if he didn't become a  warlord but that's just speculation so  we'll work with the figure that we have  luffy's own bounty like last time jumps  well past his defeated opponent's bounty  and lands at a very impressive 100  million berries this time his bounty is  about 25 percent higher than that of his  most recent defeated opponent things get  less straightforward with the next  bounty because luffy fights rob lucci  before he gets it rather than a pirate  with a measurable bounty after defeating  the marine's own man cp 9's strongest  member in history luffy's new boutique  is revealed during chapter 435 it's 300  million berries this raises another  interesting aspect about bounties the  world government issues them based on  their perceived threat level of a given  pirate so being a threat to the world  government and their established order  rather than just a strong dude who never  interferes with the marines will mean  that you get a much higher bounty in  theory so since luffy beat one of the  marine strong fighters rather than just  a pirate it's no surprise his bounty  shot up so much here this is another  aspect to keep in mind when discussing  what his newest bounty will be next  let's fast forward to chapter 601 where  luffy's fourth bounty is revealed to be  400 million this is post time skip and  marine ford where luffy helped break  prisoners out of impel down people found  out he's the world's worst criminals aka  monkey d dragon's son he escaped the war  with the help of whitebeard and shanks  and so on you might ask why his bounty  didn't go up more since this is the  smallest jump so far percentage-wise  well i'm guessing it's because he wasn't  that powerful at marine ford he failed  to rescue his brother he broke down and  he had to be saved if he succeeded at  mari